research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-5590-    87	3.1 Combining: $\kappa \le \kappa \oplus \lambda \le \kappa \oplus \kappa \le \kappa$ gives $\kappa \oplus \lambda = \kappa$ by [L6]; and for $\lambda \ne 0$, $\kappa \le \kappa \otimes \lambda \le \kappa \otimes \kappa = \kappa$ gives $\kappa \otimes \lambda = \kappa$, while $\kappa \otimes 0 = 0$ by [L3]. [step 1.1, step 1.3, step 1.4, step 2.1, L1, L3, L6] ∎
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-5591-    88	
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-5592-    89	## Remarks
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-5593-    90	
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-5594-    91	**What absorption costs.** Nothing beyond [[thm-hessenberg]]: the only extra input is the injection of step 1.2, which folds two copies of $\kappa$ into a rectangle of width $2$. So absorption is choice free wherever Hessenberg's theorem is, that is, for cardinals.
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-5595-    92	
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-5596-    93	**Why the hypothesis is $\lambda \le \kappa$ and not $\lambda < \kappa$.** The case $\lambda = \kappa$ is the interesting one and is used constantly: $\kappa \oplus \kappa = \kappa$ and $\kappa \otimes \kappa = \kappa$. Stating the corollary with $\le$ avoids a separate appeal to Hessenberg's theorem at every later use.
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-5597-    94	
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log:5598:    95	**Absorption destroys cancellation.** From $\kappa \oplus \lambda = \kappa$ for every $\lambda \le \kappa$ it follows at once that $\oplus$ cannot be cancellative on infinite cardinals, and the companion false statement [[fs-cardinal-addition-is-cancellative]] records exactly that. The same collapse does **not** reach exponentiation, where [[thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor]] gives a strict increase at every cardinal.
