research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-5794-65:**Why this item exists.** [[def-cardinal]] introduces $\lvert X \rvert$ under the
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-5795-66:hypothesis "Assume the Axiom of Choice", and it needs that hypothesis only to
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-5796-67:know that $X$ carries a well-order at all. Everything below is about
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-5797-68:well-orderable sets and is a theorem of ZF, which is what makes it possible to
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-5798-69:state Hessenberg's theorem and Tarski's theorem, one of which is choice-free and
