research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6577-    56	
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6578-    57	**Given:** ZF, with no choice principle. Write $n + 1 = n \cup \{n\}$ for the successor of $n \in \omega$ ([[def-natural-numbers]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6579-    58	
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6580-    59	[L1] The operation $\beta \mapsto \aleph_\beta$ is defined at every ordinal, takes infinite cardinal values, is strictly increasing, satisfies $\beta \le \aleph_\beta$, and is continuous at limits, meaning $\aleph_\lambda = \bigcup\{\aleph_\beta : \beta \in \lambda\}$ for limit $\lambda$ ([[cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined]], [[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]]).
