research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6673-    58	**Given:** ZF. Neither statement is assumed; the theorem asserts their equivalence. For a set $A$ and an ordinal $\kappa$ write $A \sqcup \kappa = (\{0\} \times A) \cup (\{1\} \times \kappa)$, and inside it write $a' = (0,a)$ for $a \in A$ and $\xi' = (1,\xi)$ for $\xi \in \kappa$; these tagged copies are disjoint and $a \mapsto a'$, $\xi \mapsto \xi'$ are injective.
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6674-    59	
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6675-    60	[L1] $\kappa \otimes \kappa = \kappa$, that is $\kappa \times \kappa \approx \kappa$, for every infinite cardinal $\kappa$, in ZF ([[thm-hessenberg]], [[def-cardinal-arithmetic]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6676-    61	
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6677-    62	[L2] For every set $A$ the Hartogs number $\aleph(A)$ is an ordinal admitting no injection into $A$ ([[thm-hartogs]]), and it is a cardinal ([[lem-successor-cardinal-exists]], [[def-cardinal]]).
