research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6679-    64	[L3] Over ZF the Axiom of Choice is equivalent to the well-ordering theorem ([[cor-ac-iff-well-ordering]], [[def-well-order]]); and assuming the Axiom of Choice every set carries a well-order ([[thm-well-ordering-theorem]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6680-    65	
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log:6681:    66	[L4] For a well-orderable $X$: $X \approx \lvert X \rvert$, the value is a cardinal, equinumerous sets receive the same one ([[lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set]]); a cardinal is infinite exactly when $\omega \le \kappa$ ([[thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting]]).
