research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log:6789:### FINDING 1 — thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor — choice ledger omits the arbitrary-set uses of Choice
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6790-LOCATION: Statement, lines 53–57; Remarks, line 97
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6791-QUOTE: "**Where the Axiom of Choice is and is not spent.** [[thm-cantor-powerset]] is choice free, and so is step 1.1. The hypothesis is used exactly twice, both times to know that a set has a cardinality: at $\mathcal{P}(\kappa)$ and at ${}^{\kappa}2$."
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6792-DEFECT: Step 2.1 also uses Choice to obtain cardinalities for an arbitrary set A and its power set. The assertion that Choice is used exactly twice is therefore false, and the Statement makes the same omission.
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6793-EVIDENCE: In any model of ZF where the well-ordering theorem fails, take a set A that is not well-orderable. The cited cardinality lemma cannot supply its cardinality, so the arbitrary-set passage in step 2.1 requires Choice beyond the two places named.
