research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6821-### FINDING 5 — lem-successor-cardinal-exists — ZF prose uses an unqualified cardinal power and overstates what is undecided
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6822-LOCATION: Statement, lines 55–58
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6823-QUOTE: "**What this supplies, and what it does not.** It gives a successor operation on cardinals in ZF alone: there is always a next one, and it is definable. It says nothing about how *large* the next cardinal is compared with $2^{\kappa}$; that comparison is not decided by the axioms in use here."
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6824-DEFECT: Under the library’s definition, cardinal exponentiation need not be defined in ZF. After Choice is assumed, the order comparison is decided: the successor cardinal is at most the power-set cardinal. What remains undecided is equality and the possible size of the gap.
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f2-cantor-hessenberg.log-6825-EVIDENCE: In a model of ZF where the reals are not well-orderable, take kappa to be omega; the library’s cardinal power is undefined. Under Choice, Cantor gives kappa below its power, while this item makes the successor the least cardinal above kappa, so the successor is always at most the power.
