research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-4097-    82	
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-4098-    83	**Given:** Cardinals $\kappa, \lambda, \mu$, in ZF; the Axiom of Choice is assumed only where an exponential is written and is not one of the four unit cases.
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-4099-    84	
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-4100-    85	[L1] For a well-orderable $X$, $\lvert X \rvert$ is the least ordinal equinumerous with $X$, it satisfies $X \approx \lvert X \rvert$, it is a cardinal, equinumerous sets receive the same one, and $\lvert \alpha \rvert = \alpha$ exactly when $\alpha$ is a cardinal ([[lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-4101-    86	
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log:4102:    87	[L2] $\sqcup$, $\times$ and ${}^{B}A$ respect $\approx$ in both arguments ([[lem-cardinal-operations-are-well-defined]], claim (a)).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-4103-    88	
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-4104-    89	[L3] $\kappa \oplus \lambda = \lvert \kappa \sqcup \lambda \rvert$, $\kappa \otimes \lambda = \lvert \kappa \times \lambda \rvert$, $\kappa^{\lambda} = \lvert {}^{\lambda}\kappa \rvert$, and these may be computed from any equinumerous representatives ([[def-cardinal-arithmetic]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-4105-    90	
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-4106-    91	[L4] If $A \preceq B$ and $B \preceq A$ then $A \approx B$ ([[thm-schroder-bernstein]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-4107-    92	
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-4108-    93	[L5] Ordinals are comparable, exactly one of $\alpha \in \beta$, $\alpha = \beta$, $\beta \in \alpha$ holds, $\alpha \subseteq \beta$ if and only if $\alpha \in \beta$ or $\alpha = \beta$, and $\alpha \notin \alpha$ ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-4109-    94	
