research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-7071-  a genuine three way split.
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-7072-- The least limit ordinal is $\omega$ ([[lem-omega-least-limit-ordinal]]), so the
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-7073-  distinction is invisible below $\omega$: every natural number is either $0$ or
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-7074-  a successor. That is precisely why ordinary induction on $\mathbb{N}$ needs
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-7075-  only a base case and a successor step, while induction over the ordinals needs
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-7076-  a limit clause as well.
