research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f1-cardinal-core.log-7348-    97	5.1 Apply [L7] to the well-order $(\kappa \cup \{\kappa\}, \in)$ of [L8] and to $S = \{\mu \in \kappa \cup \{\kappa\} : \mu$ is not an infinite cardinal, or $\lvert \mu \times \mu \rvert = \mu\}$: a $\mu$ below which everything lies in $S$ is in $S$, trivially if $\mu$ is not an infinite cardinal, by step 1.3 if $\mu = \omega$, and by step 4.1 otherwise; hence $S = \kappa \cup \{\kappa\}$, so $\kappa \in S$ and $\kappa \otimes \kappa = \lvert \kappa \times \kappa \rvert = \kappa$. [step 1.3, step 4.1, L7, L8] ∎
