research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log:4277:items/thm-tarski-square.md:60:[L1] $\kappa \otimes \kappa = \kappa$, that is $\kappa \times \kappa \approx \kappa$, for every infinite cardinal $\kappa$, in ZF ([[thm-hessenberg]], [[def-cardinal-arithmetic]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log:4278:items/thm-tarski-square.md:62:[L2] For every set $A$ the Hartogs number $\aleph(A)$ is an ordinal admitting no injection into $A$ ([[thm-hartogs]]), and it is a cardinal ([[lem-successor-cardinal-exists]], [[def-cardinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log:4279:items/thm-tarski-square.md:64:[L3] Over ZF the Axiom of Choice is equivalent to the well-ordering theorem ([[cor-ac-iff-well-ordering]], [[def-well-order]]); and assuming the Axiom of Choice every set carries a well-order ([[thm-well-ordering-theorem]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log:4280:items/thm-tarski-square.md:66:[L4] For a well-orderable $X$: $X \approx \lvert X \rvert$, the value is a cardinal, equinumerous sets receive the same one ([[lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set]]); a cardinal is infinite exactly when $\omega \le \kappa$ ([[thm-cardinal-arithmetic-agrees-with-finite-counting]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log:4281:items/thm-tarski-square.md:68:[L5] $\times$ respects $\approx$ ([[lem-cardinal-operations-are-well-defined]]); and for cardinals $\kappa \le \lambda$ iff $\kappa \preceq \lambda$ ([[lem-cardinal-arithmetic-basic-laws]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log:4282:items/thm-tarski-square.md:70:[L6] Ordinals: elements of ordinals are ordinals, trichotomy holds, $\alpha \subseteq \beta$ iff $\alpha \in \beta$ or $\alpha = \beta$, and every nonempty set of ordinals has an $\in$-least element ([[lem-ordinal-basics]], [[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[def-ordinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log:4283:items/thm-tarski-square.md:72:[L7] There is no injection $n \cup \{n\} \to n$ for $n \in \omega$ (claim 1 of [[lem-pigeonhole]]); a set is finite when it is equinumerous with a natural number ([[def-countable]], [[def-finite-cardinality]]).
