research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log-4291-items/cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined.md:88:[L7] $\lvert X \rvert$ is the least ordinal equinumerous with $X$, and $\lvert \alpha \rvert = \alpha$ exactly when $\alpha$ is a cardinal ([[lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set]], [[def-cardinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log:4292:items/cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined.md:90:[L8] Assuming the Axiom of Choice, $2^{\kappa} = \lvert \mathcal{P}(\kappa)\rvert$ is a cardinal and $\kappa < 2^{\kappa}$ ([[thm-cardinal-power-set-and-cantor]], [[def-cardinal-arithmetic]], [[def-axiom-of-choice]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log-4293-items/cor-the-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies-are-well-defined.md:92:[L9] Transfinite induction is available on any well-order, in particular on any set of ordinals ordered by $\in$ ([[thm-transfinite-induction]], [[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log-4294-items/thm-cardinal-comparability-iff-ac.md:59:[L1] For every set $A$ there is a least ordinal $\aleph(A)$ admitting no injection into $A$, and its construction is choice free ([[thm-hartogs]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log-4295-items/thm-cardinal-comparability-iff-ac.md:61:[L2] Over ZF the Axiom of Choice is equivalent to the well-ordering theorem, that every set can be well ordered ([[cor-ac-iff-well-ordering]], [[def-well-order]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log-4296-items/thm-cardinal-comparability-iff-ac.md:63:[L3] Assuming the Axiom of Choice, every set carries a well-order ([[thm-well-ordering-theorem]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log-4297-items/thm-cardinal-comparability-iff-ac.md:65:[L4] A set is well-orderable exactly when it is equinumerous with an ordinal, and it then has a least such ordinal $\lvert A \rvert$, with $A \approx \lvert A \rvert$ ([[lem-cardinality-of-a-well-orderable-set]], [[def-cardinal]], [[def-ordinal]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log-4298-items/thm-cardinal-comparability-iff-ac.md:67:[L5] Ordinals satisfy trichotomy and $\alpha \subseteq \beta$ iff $\alpha \in \beta$ or $\alpha = \beta$ ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log-4299-items/thm-cardinal-comparability-iff-ac.md:69:[L6] A subset inclusion is an injection, and a composition of injections and bijections is an injection ([[def-injection-surjection-bijection]]).
