research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log-5226-**(a) In ZF.** Every infinite cardinal $\kappa$ ([[def-cardinal]]) equals
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log-5227-$\aleph_\alpha$ ([[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]]) for **exactly one** ordinal
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log-5228-$\alpha$. So the alephs are not merely a supply of infinite cardinals: they are
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log-5229-all of them, and the operation $\alpha \mapsto \aleph_\alpha$ is a bijective
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log-5230-enumeration of the infinite cardinals by the ordinals.
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log-5231-
