research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log-6148-items/thm-ordinal-arithmetic-monotonicity.md:143:**No completeness is assumed.** Every supremum here is a union of a set of ordinals, an ordinal by claim (e) of [[lem-ordinal-basics]]. The ordinals are closed under suprema of sets for free, which is what makes the limit clauses legitimate in the first place.
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log-6149-items/cor-cofinality-of-a-cardinal-power.md:71:[L10] Ordinals satisfy trichotomy, $\alpha \subseteq \beta$ iff $\alpha \in \beta$ or $\alpha = \beta$, the union of a set of ordinals is its least upper bound, and every nonempty set of ordinals has an $\in$-least element; a function is injective when equality of two values forces equality of the corresponding inputs ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]], [[def-well-order]], [[def-injection-surjection-bijection]]).
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-refuter-refute-f3-hierarchies-ac.log-6150-items/thm-regularity-of-the-alephs.md:75:[L9] Ordinals satisfy trichotomy, $\alpha \subseteq \beta$ iff $\alpha \in \beta$ or $\alpha = \beta$, the union of a set of ordinals is its least upper bound, every nonempty set of ordinals has an $\in$-least element, $\omega$ is the least limit ordinal, and every strictly increasing map of ordinals is injective ([[lem-ordinal-trichotomy]], [[lem-ordinal-basics]], [[lem-omega-least-limit-ordinal]], [[def-injection-surjection-bijection]]).
